# Copy to .env.local for local development (it is git-ignored), or add these in Vercel:
# Project > Settings > Environment Variables (Production, and Preview if previews should deliver too).
# None of these is ever sent to the browser. See docs/the-wed-theory.md, "Receiving enquiries".

# --- Email every enquiry to the studio inbox through Resend (recommended) ---
# A Resend API key with "Sending access". Secret: mark it Sensitive in Vercel.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# The inbox that receives enquiries. Several can be separated by commas.
ENQUIRY_EMAIL_TO=
# Optional. Without it, Resend's shared test sender is used, which can only deliver to the address
# the Resend account was created with. To send from your own domain, verify it at Resend first.
# ENQUIRY_EMAIL_FROM=The Wed Theory <enquiries@yourdomain.com>

# --- And/or post every enquiry as JSON to a webhook (Formspree, Make, Zapier, n8n, a CRM) ---
# Must be https:// (http://localhost is allowed for testing).
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional. Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# --- Site address ---
# Optional. Share previews, canonical links, sitemap.xml and robots.txt use it. Without it the
# production domain Vercel assigns is used, then http://localhost:3000.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thewedtheory.com
